[{"sha":"6e5b8b7e4d88b0cdbfab6d2e6bc531cddab46065","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDZlNWI4YjdlNGQ4OGIwY2RiZmFiNmQyZTZiYzUzMWNkZGFiNDYwNjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T14:00:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:35Z"},"message":"gguf: add qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) arch and converter\n\nAdds the GGUF-side plumbing for HF model_type qwen4_exp:\n\n- MODEL_ARCH.QWEN4EXP plus tensors for the low-rank hyper-connection\n  variant (hc_*_norm/down/up/inject) and the PLE n-gram hash embeddings.\n  The DeepSeek-V4 hc_*_fn/base/scale tensors are a different\n  parameterisation, so these are separate entries rather than reuse.\n- Reuses the existing indexer, per_layer_token_embd, SSM and\n  compress_ratios keys unchanged.\n- conversion/qwen4exp.py inherits the Qwen3.5 linear-attention V-head\n  reorder and interleaved mrope, concatenates the 128 PLE embedding\n  shards, and splits index_qk_proj into separate indexer q/k tensors.\n\nThe PLE hash multipliers reach ~2.4e13. prepare_tensors() casts every\nnon-float dtype to float32 before modify_tensors() runs, and GGUF array\nwrites infer INT32 from Python ints, so both paths are bypassed: the\nconstants are read from the pre-cast lazy tensors and written as\nexplicit UINT64 arrays.\n\nAdditive only; no existing arch changes behaviour.","tree":{"sha":"d16a5ecaf8f102debc10288f48016e46ab202a93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/d16a5ecaf8f102debc10288f48016e46ab202a93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/6e5b8b7e4d88b0cdbfab6d2e6bc531cddab46065","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6e5b8b7e4d88b0cdbfab6d2e6bc531cddab46065","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/6e5b8b7e4d88b0cdbfab6d2e6bc531cddab46065","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6e5b8b7e4d88b0cdbfab6d2e6bc531cddab46065/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4d19b287691e8f47fc303be420f630c40ec45684","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/4d19b287691e8f47fc303be420f630c40ec45684","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/4d19b287691e8f47fc303be420f630c40ec45684"}]},{"sha":"331fa7e56091a06a1b557987f050a7cd3b77ca33","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDMzMWZhN2U1NjA5MWEwNmExYjU1Nzk4N2YwNTBhN2NkM2I3N2NhMzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T14:09:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:35Z"},"message":"llama: load qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) hparams and tensors\n\nAdds LLM_ARCH_QWEN4EXP with its hparams and tensor loading. The graph\ncomes in the next commit; this makes the model load and report correct\nmetadata.\n\n- hyper-connections set n_embd_out_impl = hc_count * n_embd, so the\n  residual stream is 4x wide and there is no output_norm: the final\n  mixer's hc_norm is the last norm in the model.\n- registered as hybrid and given the same recurrent/attention memory\n  filters as Qwen3-Next and Qwen3.5.\n- reuses the existing indexer, per_layer_token_embd, SSM and\n  compress_ratios keys as-is.\n- the PLE table row count is read back from the file rather than\n  recomputing the vocab padding rule.\n\nllama-model-loader gains UINT64 array support. That branch previously\nthrew, so no existing caller changes behaviour; it is needed because the\nPLE hash multipliers do not fit in int32.","tree":{"sha":"78da66653711d4d042ea9eb3d9107041a4c9e967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/78da66653711d4d042ea9eb3d9107041a4c9e967"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/331fa7e56091a06a1b557987f050a7cd3b77ca33","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/331fa7e56091a06a1b557987f050a7cd3b77ca33","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/331fa7e56091a06a1b557987f050a7cd3b77ca33","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/331fa7e56091a06a1b557987f050a7cd3b77ca33/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6e5b8b7e4d88b0cdbfab6d2e6bc531cddab46065","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6e5b8b7e4d88b0cdbfab6d2e6bc531cddab46065","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/6e5b8b7e4d88b0cdbfab6d2e6bc531cddab46065"}]},{"sha":"058b7a1b48ccdb4d1df60f1d94ef904990082bef","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDA1OGI3YTFiNDhjY2RiNGQxZGY2MGYxZDk0ZWY5MDQ5OTAwODJiZWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T12:37:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:35Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: shorten comments","tree":{"sha":"06d926d0dcbb2eb3021f6701f23742dae78b26e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/06d926d0dcbb2eb3021f6701f23742dae78b26e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/058b7a1b48ccdb4d1df60f1d94ef904990082bef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/058b7a1b48ccdb4d1df60f1d94ef904990082bef","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/058b7a1b48ccdb4d1df60f1d94ef904990082bef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/058b7a1b48ccdb4d1df60f1d94ef904990082bef/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"331fa7e56091a06a1b557987f050a7cd3b77ca33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/331fa7e56091a06a1b557987f050a7cd3b77ca33","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/331fa7e56091a06a1b557987f050a7cd3b77ca33"}]},{"sha":"c9ad86f6b92ac467621bf8706c77dc0b053ba7a2","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGM5YWQ4NmY2YjkyYWM0Njc2MjFiZjg3MDZjNzdkYzBiMDUzYmE3YTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T14:51:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:35Z"},"message":"llama: qwen4exp text graph with hyper-connections, GDN and MoE\n\nImplements the decode graph for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: the hyper-connection\nresidual stream, gated delta net layers, the MoE block with its gated shared\nexpert, and dense full attention. The QSA indexer and the PLE n-gram embedding\nare not wired up yet and land in later commits.\n\nHyper-connections are implemented here rather than shared with deepseek4.cpp.\nThe two formulations agree on the [n_embd, hc, n_tokens] layout and little\nelse: DeepSeek-V4 mixes with a full-rank projection and Sinkhorn-normalises\nit, whereas this model uses a low-rank down/silu/up sigmoid gate and collapses\nby a plain mean. Only the ~10 line stream mean is genuinely common, so sharing\nwould mean touching DSV4's hot path and its three fused CUDA ops to reuse very\nlittle. What is reused is the substantive part: the LLM_KV_HYPER_CONNECTION_*\nkeys, the n_embd_out_impl wide-residual support already in the loader, and the\nlayout convention.\n\nAlso allows a checkpoint to carry no PLE layers at all, which makes it\npossible to bring the graph up and validate it in stages.\n\nValidated against vLLM, the only working reference implementation. On a\nscaled-down model with an init scale large enough to give non-uniform logits,\nagreement with vLLM sits at the numerical noise floor: llama.cpp f32 against\nits own bf16 gives 84.3% top-1 agreement over 255 positions, and this graph\nagainst vLLM gives 85.1%. The comparison was calibrated by seeding three\ndeliberate bugs (silu instead of sigmoid on the delta net gate, dropping the\n1/hc scale in the mix, dropping the 2x in the combine); each drops top-1 to\nbetween 0% and 11%, an order of magnitude below the floor.","tree":{"sha":"5da7fa9e699f117566ade5e8d16ed7e9f67ef7fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/5da7fa9e699f117566ade5e8d16ed7e9f67ef7fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/c9ad86f6b92ac467621bf8706c77dc0b053ba7a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c9ad86f6b92ac467621bf8706c77dc0b053ba7a2","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/c9ad86f6b92ac467621bf8706c77dc0b053ba7a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c9ad86f6b92ac467621bf8706c77dc0b053ba7a2/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"058b7a1b48ccdb4d1df60f1d94ef904990082bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/058b7a1b48ccdb4d1df60f1d94ef904990082bef","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/058b7a1b48ccdb4d1df60f1d94ef904990082bef"}]},{"sha":"ad4fa3fa7be10fc2a0b19b7a74b647d023d50153","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGFkNGZhM2ZhN2JlMTBmYzJhMGIxOWI3YTc0YjY0N2QwMjNkNTAxNTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T15:15:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:35Z"},"message":"llama: qwen4exp PLE n-gram hash embedding\n\nAdds the per-layer embedding: a custom I32 graph input hashes each token with\nits ngram_size-1 predecessors host-side and the result is a plain row gather\nover the shared table, the same shape gemma3n's per-layer embedding uses. The\nhash has to run on the host because the splitmix64-derived multipliers reach\n2^45, so the products need 64-bit integers and an xor, neither of which ggml\nhas.\n\nPredecessors that fall outside the ubatch come from a small per-sequence\nhistory on the model, mirroring the per-request ngram_context the reference\ncarries. It is only trusted when contiguous with the incoming position, so a\nfresh prompt or a rewound cache falls back to EOS padding rather than hashing\nagainst stale tokens.\n\nThe depthwise conv is written out as a sum of shifted, per-channel-scaled\ncopies rather than through ggml_conv_1d_dw, which carries a correctness\nwarning upstream.\n\nVerified two ways. The row indices match a transcription of the reference's\ntensor formulation exactly, 1024 of 1024 rows, including sequences with EOS\ntokens sprinkled through them to exercise the segment reset. Separately, with\nPLE placed on layer 0 so its input is just the token embedding, ple_embd and\nple_gated_value match a PyTorch computation from the same checkpoint to every\nprinted digit.\n\nEnd to end over 1023 scored positions the port sits the same distance from\nvLLM with PLE as without it, 6.3 points of top-1 against 6.0, so PLE costs no\naccuracy relative to the rest of the model. That common offset is vLLM's bf16\nactivations, which cannot be removed: its QSA kernel refuses float32.\n\nTwo bugs found along the way, both caught by the row-index check. The history\nwas read and updated in the same pass, so a token early in a ubatch could pick\nup an earlier token of that same ubatch as prior context; it is now snapshotted\nfirst. And an EOS token was cutting its own context, where the reference takes\nthe last EOS strictly before the position, so a boundary only hides tokens from\nthe positions after it.\n\nKnown gap: the conv carries no state across ubatches, so it is exact only for a\nprefill that starts at position 0. Chunked prefill and decode need the conv\nstate wired into the recurrent memory, and the conv branch itself is still\nnumerically unverified because the fixture zeroes its weights.","tree":{"sha":"b1deb1bc6bf9e219b5f84d9f513dda1916611565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/b1deb1bc6bf9e219b5f84d9f513dda1916611565"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/ad4fa3fa7be10fc2a0b19b7a74b647d023d50153","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ad4fa3fa7be10fc2a0b19b7a74b647d023d50153","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/ad4fa3fa7be10fc2a0b19b7a74b647d023d50153","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ad4fa3fa7be10fc2a0b19b7a74b647d023d50153/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c9ad86f6b92ac467621bf8706c77dc0b053ba7a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c9ad86f6b92ac467621bf8706c77dc0b053ba7a2","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/c9ad86f6b92ac467621bf8706c77dc0b053ba7a2"}]},{"sha":"c89e67b08e5a15beeac590431b0aff8bca7891bc","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGM4OWU2N2IwOGU1YTE1YmVlYWM1OTA0MzFiMGFmZjhiY2E3ODkxYmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T15:21:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:35Z"},"message":"llama: carry the qwen4exp PLE conv state across ubatches\n\nThe PLE depthwise conv was zero-padding on the left, which is only right for a\nprefill that starts at position 0. Decode and chunked prefill saw a truncated\nhistory for the first (kernel-1)*ngram_size positions of every ubatch.\n\nThe PLE module sits on a layer that is also a delta-net layer, so both need a\nconv history in the same recurrent row. Rather than plumb a per-layer state\nsize through build_rs and build_conv_state, the row is widened once and each\nconvolution addresses its own slice through a local helper. n_embd_r() gains\nthe extra span, which is zero for every other architecture because it is\nderived from ple_n_heads.\n\nVerified by feeding the same 1024 token sequence in chunks instead of one\nshot: at 64 tokens per decode the logits are bit-identical to the single-shot\nrun, 1023 of 1023 top-1 and a maximum logprob deviation of exactly zero. At\none token per decode they differ slightly, but the no-PLE model differs more\nunder the same test (94.6% against 97.1%), so that is the usual gemv-versus-\ngemm accumulation difference and not the state.\n\nThe conv branch is also no longer unverified. With non-zero conv weights the\nport sits 6.3 points of top-1 below the numerical floor, the same distance as\nwith the weights zeroed and as the model with no PLE at all, so the branch\nadds no error of its own.\n\ntest-llama-archs passes every existing architecture at 0.00e+00, including the\ndelta-net models that share this code path.","tree":{"sha":"6ec7c2e3499a57a5414905f52e124fe58eeaca99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/6ec7c2e3499a57a5414905f52e124fe58eeaca99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/c89e67b08e5a15beeac590431b0aff8bca7891bc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c89e67b08e5a15beeac590431b0aff8bca7891bc","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/c89e67b08e5a15beeac590431b0aff8bca7891bc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c89e67b08e5a15beeac590431b0aff8bca7891bc/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ad4fa3fa7be10fc2a0b19b7a74b647d023d50153","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ad4fa3fa7be10fc2a0b19b7a74b647d023d50153","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/ad4fa3fa7be10fc2a0b19b7a74b647d023d50153"}]},{"sha":"ddf0980e52ae176b46ab189f2a63f53f24c4186e","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGRkZjA5ODBlNTJhZTE3NmI0NmFiMTg5ZjJhNjNmNTNmMjRjNDE4NmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T15:29:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:52Z"},"message":"llama: fix the qwen4exp PLE conv state and unblock test-llama-archs\n\nbuild_rs writes into the state tensor in place, zeroing one row and copying the\ncarried-over states, so calling it twice for the same layer let the second call\nclobber the first write-back. The PLE layer is also a delta-net layer, so that\nis exactly what happened: both convolutions gathered the same row. They now\nshare a single gather per layer.\n\nThe earlier claim that the conv state was carried correctly was tested on a\nfixture whose conv weights are zero, where the branch contributes nothing and\nchunking matches trivially. Re-running with non-zero conv weights showed the\ndivergence, growing with the number of ubatch boundaries: 97.1% top-1 at one\nboundary down to 90.2% at seven. With the shared gather it is bit-identical to\nthe single-shot run at every chunk size tried, 512, 128 and 64, with a maximum\nlogprob deviation of exactly zero over 1023 positions. The delta-net-only model\nstays bit-identical too, so nothing regressed there.\n\nAlso derive the delta-net conv channel count the way load_arch_tensors sizes\nwqkv instead of from ssm_d_inner. The two agree for this model, but n_embd_r()\nonly bounds the row and the convolution has to match the tensor feeding it.\n\ntest-llama-archs previously aborted on this architecture and took every later\narchitecture with it. qwen4exp is marked MoE-only, given the hyper-connection\nkeys and an ssm_d_inner consistent with its tensor derivation, and skipped for\nnow: the hyper-connection keys written by get_gguf_ctx are not reaching the\nsynthesised file, which needs a separate look. The suite completes again, 124\narchitectures at 0.00e+00.","tree":{"sha":"fab635e5e03087dfc7d1babfc5887c73adba91dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/fab635e5e03087dfc7d1babfc5887c73adba91dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/ddf0980e52ae176b46ab189f2a63f53f24c4186e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ddf0980e52ae176b46ab189f2a63f53f24c4186e","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/ddf0980e52ae176b46ab189f2a63f53f24c4186e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ddf0980e52ae176b46ab189f2a63f53f24c4186e/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c89e67b08e5a15beeac590431b0aff8bca7891bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c89e67b08e5a15beeac590431b0aff8bca7891bc","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/c89e67b08e5a15beeac590431b0aff8bca7891bc"}]},{"sha":"ff24f3874f1de472a5494338cf2832ce982a320e","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGZmMjRmMzg3NGYxZGU0NzJhNTQ5NDMzOGNmMjgzMmNlOTgyYTMyMGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T18:16:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:52Z"},"message":"llama: optional indexer key cache in llama_memory_hybrid\n\nGroundwork for qwen4exp's QSA sparse attention. Its indexer needs a per-token\nkey history for the full-attention layers, but a hybrid model cannot use\nllama_kv_cache_dsa: that class derives from llama_memory_i rather than\nllama_kv_cache, and llama_memory_hybrid constructs its attention cache\ndirectly. No existing architecture pairs recurrent state with a sparse\nindexer, so there was nothing to reuse wholesale.\n\nllama_memory_hybrid therefore gains a third, optional cache, shaped the same\nway llama_kv_cache_dsa shapes its lightning-indexer cache: a copy of hparams\nwith n_head_kv forced to 1 and n_embd_head_k_full set to indexer_head_size.\nIt is built only when a filter_idx callback is passed, which defaults to\nnullptr, so every existing architecture gets exactly what it got before. The\nper-sequence operations and the batch preparation forward to it under a null\ncheck, matching how the DSA cache prepares its two caches over the same\nubatches.\n\ntest-llama-archs passes all 124 architectures at 0.00e+00, including the 12 in\nthe hybrid family that share this code. The qwen4exp fixtures are unchanged:\nsame logits against vLLM, and chunked evaluation still bit-identical to\nsingle-shot.","tree":{"sha":"243a6848faa329501d5d15c6ddc2437599e733ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/243a6848faa329501d5d15c6ddc2437599e733ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/ff24f3874f1de472a5494338cf2832ce982a320e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ff24f3874f1de472a5494338cf2832ce982a320e","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/ff24f3874f1de472a5494338cf2832ce982a320e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ff24f3874f1de472a5494338cf2832ce982a320e/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ddf0980e52ae176b46ab189f2a63f53f24c4186e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ddf0980e52ae176b46ab189f2a63f53f24c4186e","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/ddf0980e52ae176b46ab189f2a63f53f24c4186e"}]},{"sha":"c88c916636611afb93f0ea6aa17a8b0edb6c5760","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGM4OGM5MTY2MzY2MTFhZmI5M2YwZWE2YWExN2E4YjBlZGI2YzU3NjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T19:09:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:52Z"},"message":"llama: QSA sparse attention for qwen4exp\n\nThe full-attention layers of this model do not attend to everything. An\nindexer scores one mean-pooled key per block of compress_ratio tokens and\nkeeps a budget of the best blocks, plus the tail of tokens that do not yet\nform a complete block. Below indexer_top_k + compress_ratio - 1 cached\ntokens every block fits in the budget, so the result is exactly dense.\n\nWhat is reused rather than rebuilt:\n\n  - the mask machinery. build_attn's DSA overload already turns a list of\n    token indices into a KQ mask via ggml_set_rows, so that block is lifted\n    out verbatim into build_attn_mask_top_k and shared with a new overload\n    on llm_graph_input_attn_kv. DSA's node sequence is unchanged; the new\n    overload exists because llama_kv_cache_dsa assumes MLA and cannot be\n    dropped into a hybrid model.\n  - the indexer key cache, which is the optional third cache added to\n    llama_memory_hybrid in the previous commit. It holds raw keys, because\n    pooling happens before the norm and the rotation.\n\nThe graph expands block scores rather than block indices: giving every\ntoken of a block its block's score needs only a gather, where expanding\nindices would need an integer multiply-add that ggml has no op for. Since\nthe budget is a whole number of blocks and a block's members tie exactly,\nthe cut still lands on a block boundary.\n\nEverything that depends on cache layout is computed host-side in\nset_input_qsa. Blocks are cuts of the position line rather than of the cell\narray, so nothing assumes the cache is contiguous.\n\nMeasured on the tiny fixture against vLLM, comparing the selected token\nindices directly rather than the logits:\n\n  below the budget    selection identical, and 1024-token logits are\n                      bit-identical to the pre-QSA dense path\n  above the budget    mean jaccard 0.975\n\nThe direct index comparison is what made this correct. The reference\nrectifies each head's dot product before summing over heads, which an\nearlier reading of it had missed; on logits alone the resulting port looked\nfine, because on a randomly initialised fixture the known-correct dense\npath already disagrees with vLLM by more than the bug did. Comparing the\nindices showed 0.794, and fixing the ReLU moved it to 0.975.","tree":{"sha":"34c21cd0e62870d5faf039a32878cd87b8aafae1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/34c21cd0e62870d5faf039a32878cd87b8aafae1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/c88c916636611afb93f0ea6aa17a8b0edb6c5760","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c88c916636611afb93f0ea6aa17a8b0edb6c5760","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/c88c916636611afb93f0ea6aa17a8b0edb6c5760","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c88c916636611afb93f0ea6aa17a8b0edb6c5760/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ff24f3874f1de472a5494338cf2832ce982a320e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ff24f3874f1de472a5494338cf2832ce982a320e","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/ff24f3874f1de472a5494338cf2832ce982a320e"}]},{"sha":"1b599101d20dcea6505ec76dae90ed451535eba8","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDFiNTk5MTAxZDIwZGNlYTY1MDVlYzc2ZGFlOTBlZDQ1MTUzNWViYTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T21:07:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:52Z"},"message":"llama: give the qwen4exp indexer cache the attention cache's slots\n\nThe indexer cache found its own slots, independently of the attention\ncache. Both are the same size and see the same ubatches, so in a\nstraight-through prefill they agree, which is why every fixture and every\nsingle-shot parity run passed. They drift once the context is being\nrewritten between turns, and then the QSA top-k indices, which are applied\nagainst the attention mask, point at the wrong cells.\n\nThe seven-turn chat test caught it on the third turn: llama-server aborted\non the assertion that the two caches report the same n_kv.\n\nThe cache is a side buffer addressed by the attention cache's cells, so it\nnow takes that cache's slot layout instead of computing one. Applying that\nlayout also marks its cells identically, so the two agree cell for cell by\nconstruction rather than by coincidence, and the assertion can no longer\nfire.\n\nInert where the caches already agreed: test-llama-archs green at 126 archs\nand 0.00e+00, and the 4096-token tiny fixture is unchanged at max logit\ndelta 0.0.","tree":{"sha":"779246e4aa0cffd5094345e21831626a3d891e35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/779246e4aa0cffd5094345e21831626a3d891e35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/1b599101d20dcea6505ec76dae90ed451535eba8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/1b599101d20dcea6505ec76dae90ed451535eba8","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/1b599101d20dcea6505ec76dae90ed451535eba8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/1b599101d20dcea6505ec76dae90ed451535eba8/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c88c916636611afb93f0ea6aa17a8b0edb6c5760","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c88c916636611afb93f0ea6aa17a8b0edb6c5760","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/c88c916636611afb93f0ea6aa17a8b0edb6c5760"}]},{"sha":"dd8962766fddcf20341a214181dfd28eabb43685","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGRkODk2Mjc2NmZkZGNmMjAzNDFhMjE0MTgxZGZkMjhlYWJiNDM2ODU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T19:09:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:40:52Z"},"message":"tests: record what the qwen4exp arch-test skip actually observes\n\nThe old note guessed that the hyper-connection keys never reach the file.\nThey do: dumping the gguf_context handed to llama_model_init_from_user\nshows both among its 67 KVs, and the loader still reports one missing.","tree":{"sha":"e37e48f39a3b4a241cca02c7d5401910f8d03d4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/e37e48f39a3b4a241cca02c7d5401910f8d03d4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/dd8962766fddcf20341a214181dfd28eabb43685","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/dd8962766fddcf20341a214181dfd28eabb43685","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/dd8962766fddcf20341a214181dfd28eabb43685","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/dd8962766fddcf20341a214181dfd28eabb43685/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1b599101d20dcea6505ec76dae90ed451535eba8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/1b599101d20dcea6505ec76dae90ed451535eba8","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/1b599101d20dcea6505ec76dae90ed451535eba8"}]},{"sha":"40e90413fd47ccff5519d3400c1ad4aa7ca39242","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDQwZTkwNDEzZmQ0N2NjZmY1NTE5ZDM0MDBjMWFkNGFhN2NhMzkyNDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T19:17:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:41:50Z"},"message":"tests: cover qwen4exp in test-llama-archs\n\nThe arch was skipped with a note guessing that the hyper-connection keys\nnever reached the synthesised file. They did. The suite builds a model, then\nsaves and reloads it, and llama_model_saver did not re-emit those keys, so\nthe failure was in the roundtrip leg rather than the first load. Three gaps,\nall in shared code and all additive:\n\n  - add_kv_from_model wrote no hyper-connection, compress-ratio or PLE keys.\n    The PLE group only means anything whole, so it is written or omitted\n    together; the rest follow the file's existing style of writing every key\n    unconditionally, since an architecture that does not read one is\n    unaffected by a zero.\n  - the saver had no uint64 path at all, which the PLE hash constants need.\n  - add_tensors_from_model enumerates model-level tensors by hand and was\n    missing per_layer_tok_embd and the three final-mixer tensors.\n\nTwo smaller fixes on the qwen4exp side, both found by running the test:\n\n  - build_qsa_top_k divided by the compression ratio before asserting it was\n    non-zero, so a file without the key crashed instead of reporting.\n  - a layer with no compression ratio now falls back to dense attention,\n    which is what the model computes below the budget anyway. The test then\n    has to write a ratio to reach QSA at all, and an indexer key length no\n    narrower than n_rot, since the indexer ropes with the main attention's\n    rotary width.\n\nFull suite: 126 archs, qwen4exp at 0.00e+00 with roundtrip OK. The tiny\nfixture is unchanged, max logit delta 0.0 against the pre-QSA dense run.","tree":{"sha":"9927c5f9e59e8c006d56e7ee41b9001685d278f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/9927c5f9e59e8c006d56e7ee41b9001685d278f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/40e90413fd47ccff5519d3400c1ad4aa7ca39242","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/40e90413fd47ccff5519d3400c1ad4aa7ca39242","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/40e90413fd47ccff5519d3400c1ad4aa7ca39242","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/40e90413fd47ccff5519d3400c1ad4aa7ca39242/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dd8962766fddcf20341a214181dfd28eabb43685","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/dd8962766fddcf20341a214181dfd28eabb43685","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/dd8962766fddcf20341a214181dfd28eabb43685"}]},{"sha":"53c0f624ae01ab8d8db9d1afbe34fa62ba8d50b9","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDUzYzBmNjI0YWUwMWFiOGQ4ZGI5ZDFhZmJlMzRmYTYyYmE4ZDUwYjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-25T19:21:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:41:50Z"},"message":"convert: stream the qwen4exp PLE table instead of concatenating it\n\nThe n-gram table arrives as 128 shards that were held in a dict and then\ntorch.cat-ed, so the peak was the shards plus the concatenation: around\n300 GB of RSS on the real checkpoint, which rules out machines that could\notherwise convert this model.\n\nEach shard is now written straight into a memory-mapped file at its final\nrow offset and dropped, so the resident set is one shard and the rest is\nthe page cache's problem. The temporary file sits beside the output and is\nremoved once the write finishes, including on failure.\n\nShards other than the last must be uniform for direct placement, which is\nasserted rather than assumed, and a shard arriving before the stride is\nknown is held instead of misplaced.\n\nVerified on the tiny fixture: the resulting GGUF is byte-identical to the\none the concatenating path produced (md5 2d274efac91ad1e9a6007efb0687e597).","tree":{"sha":"baa6842760dd6fc619c63dbec7b6f181f4e89501","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/baa6842760dd6fc619c63dbec7b6f181f4e89501"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/53c0f624ae01ab8d8db9d1afbe34fa62ba8d50b9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/53c0f624ae01ab8d8db9d1afbe34fa62ba8d50b9","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/53c0f624ae01ab8d8db9d1afbe34fa62ba8d50b9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/53c0f624ae01ab8d8db9d1afbe34fa62ba8d50b9/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"40e90413fd47ccff5519d3400c1ad4aa7ca39242","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/40e90413fd47ccff5519d3400c1ad4aa7ca39242","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/40e90413fd47ccff5519d3400c1ad4aa7ca39242"}]},{"sha":"570c26d3d6f386e3564a1dd949c08ac99da5e7cf","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDU3MGMyNmQzZDZmMzg2ZTM1NjRhMWRkOTQ5YzA4YWM5OWRhNWU3Y2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"danielhanchen@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-25T23:18:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:41:50Z"},"message":"quantize: fall back to F16 for 32-block types with an odd ncols\n\ntensor_type_fallback demotes a tensor whose ncols is not a multiple of the\ntarget's block size, but its switch only enumerates the 256-block types. A\ntarget that is already a 32-block type (iq4_nl, q4_0, q5_0, q8_0, ...) falls\ninto default: and throws, even though the function already knows how to answer\nthat case: the ncols check right below the switch resolves an unrepresentable\nshape to F16.\n\nRoute those types into that check instead of throwing. Only paths that abort\ntoday change, so no quantization that currently succeeds is affected.\n\nFound on a 4-wide depthwise conv kernel. llama-quantize reported nothing but\n\"failed to quantize model from ...\", with no tensor name and no exception text,\nwhich made a quant recipe that had simply not pinned the tensor look like a\ncorrupt model. It now names the tensor and continues.","tree":{"sha":"8b1f1f067b219322923310e5600caf634c12e4d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/8b1f1f067b219322923310e5600caf634c12e4d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/570c26d3d6f386e3564a1dd949c08ac99da5e7cf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/570c26d3d6f386e3564a1dd949c08ac99da5e7cf","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/570c26d3d6f386e3564a1dd949c08ac99da5e7cf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/570c26d3d6f386e3564a1dd949c08ac99da5e7cf/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"53c0f624ae01ab8d8db9d1afbe34fa62ba8d50b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/53c0f624ae01ab8d8db9d1afbe34fa62ba8d50b9","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/53c0f624ae01ab8d8db9d1afbe34fa62ba8d50b9"}]},{"sha":"4597a86f124e2ef04676fa9a6cb989235d2ac63c","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDQ1OTdhODZmMTI0ZTJlZjA0Njc2ZmE5YTZjYjk4OTIzNWQyYWM2M2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"danielhanchen@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-25T23:28:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:41:50Z"},"message":"quantize: let --tensor-type name per_layer_token_embd\n\nper_layer_token_embd shares the TOKEN_EMBD category with token_embd.weight, so\n--token-embedding-type is returned for it before any --tensor-type pattern is\nconsulted, and there is no way to give it a tier of its own.\n\nThat grouping is fine as a default and stays the default. It is a poor fit for\nthe size, though: on qwen4exp the table is 97.7 GiB of a 337.6 GiB BF16 file and\nabout 46% of a 4-bit one, roughly eighty times token_embd.weight, and it is\nread by ggml_get_rows rather than a matmul so no imatrix ever covers it.\n\nAllow an explicit --tensor-type pattern to name it, and only it. Nothing\nchanges unless such a pattern is passed, and token_embd.weight keeps the old\nprecedence in either case.\n\nMeasured on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, Q4_K_M with an imatrix: the table lands at q8_0\n(51.9 GiB, 113.5 GiB total) by following --token-embedding-type, and pinning it\nq4_1 gives 30.5 GiB for 92.1 GiB total, 19% off the file.","tree":{"sha":"cb9422f1b0ee4428d72a438143ec5be9fac34816","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/cb9422f1b0ee4428d72a438143ec5be9fac34816"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/4597a86f124e2ef04676fa9a6cb989235d2ac63c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/4597a86f124e2ef04676fa9a6cb989235d2ac63c","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/4597a86f124e2ef04676fa9a6cb989235d2ac63c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/4597a86f124e2ef04676fa9a6cb989235d2ac63c/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"570c26d3d6f386e3564a1dd949c08ac99da5e7cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/570c26d3d6f386e3564a1dd949c08ac99da5e7cf","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/570c26d3d6f386e3564a1dd949c08ac99da5e7cf"}]},{"sha":"25aa77a4e2ad491b511e223f2de5950b7e1946ee","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDI1YWE3N2E0ZTJhZDQ5MWI1MTFlMjIzZjJkZTU5NTBiN2UxOTQ2ZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"danielhanchen@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-26T00:31:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:41:50Z"},"message":"quantize: size the output buffer exactly instead of nelements * 4\n\nThe per-tensor output buffer was sized `nelements * 4`, described as an upper\nbound. It is a very loose one: the output is at most 2 bytes per element\n(f16/bf16) and usually well under 1.1 (q8_0 and below), so between 2x and 4x of\nit is never touched. The exact size is already known here, since it is what the\nquantization loop writes, what new_size sums to, and what the GGUF metadata is\nasserted against a few lines later.\n\nOn a model whose largest tensor is a few GB none of this matters. On\nQwen3.8-Flash-Next it does: per_layer_token_embd is 51.2 G elements, so the\nbuffer was 205 GB where 54 GB is needed at q8_0 and 32 GB at q4_1.\n\nMeasured on that model, VmHWM of a live llama-quantize was 485 GB per process.\nThree of them fit in 2 TB and five did not, which is what an OOM-killed quant\nladder looks like. This removes about 150 GB of that.\n\nByte-identical output, verified against the same binary built at the parent\ncommit: q4_K, q8_0, q5_K, q6_K and IQ4_XS, over BF16 and F32 sources, with and\nwithout a PLE table present. Six cases, six matching md5s.","tree":{"sha":"3b470f3343ed6c91dce960b5587f8a1536605f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/3b470f3343ed6c91dce960b5587f8a1536605f96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/25aa77a4e2ad491b511e223f2de5950b7e1946ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/25aa77a4e2ad491b511e223f2de5950b7e1946ee","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/25aa77a4e2ad491b511e223f2de5950b7e1946ee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/25aa77a4e2ad491b511e223f2de5950b7e1946ee/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4597a86f124e2ef04676fa9a6cb989235d2ac63c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/4597a86f124e2ef04676fa9a6cb989235d2ac63c","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/4597a86f124e2ef04676fa9a6cb989235d2ac63c"}]},{"sha":"eb95d125bad0b8d302717a7a55e61845da9e7883","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGViOTVkMTI1YmFkMGI4ZDMwMjcxN2E3YTU1ZTYxODQ1ZGE5ZTc4ODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"danielhanchen@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-26T00:58:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:41:50Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: hash the image placeholder for multimodal batches\n\nThe PLE row indices are computed host-side from ubatch->token, and set_input\nreturned early when that was null. A multimodal ubatch is exactly that case:\nthe mtmd layer consumes the image placeholder ids and hands llama_decode\nembeddings instead. The early return left the I32 index tensor uninitialised,\nso ggml_get_rows indexed a 320 M row table with whatever the buffer happened to\ncontain, and aborted:\n\n  GGML_ASSERT(i01 >= 0 && i01 < ne01) failed\n    ggml_compute_forward_get_rows\n    mtmd_helper_decode_image_chunk -> llama_decode\n\nEvery image request crashed. Nothing caught it because the vision work had only\never been verified by converting an mmproj, never by running one.\n\nThe reference computes the hash over input_ids, where those positions still\nhold the image placeholder, so carry that id through as qwen4exp.ple.image_token_id\nand hash it. The key is optional: a file converted before it existed falls back\nto the PLE EOS token, which is defined and treats the image as a segment\nboundary rather than crashing.\n\nVerified end to end with llama-mtmd-cli, a Q4_K_M base and the F16 mmproj, on a\ngenerated image with known content. The model names the red circle, the blue\nsquare, the inverted green triangle and reads \"UNSLOTH 42\", each with the right\nposition.","tree":{"sha":"9dda000e6f00d61efd731735620cd7e8a27fd2df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/9dda000e6f00d61efd731735620cd7e8a27fd2df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/eb95d125bad0b8d302717a7a55e61845da9e7883","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/eb95d125bad0b8d302717a7a55e61845da9e7883","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/eb95d125bad0b8d302717a7a55e61845da9e7883","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/eb95d125bad0b8d302717a7a55e61845da9e7883/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"25aa77a4e2ad491b511e223f2de5950b7e1946ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/25aa77a4e2ad491b511e223f2de5950b7e1946ee","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/25aa77a4e2ad491b511e223f2de5950b7e1946ee"}]},{"sha":"bea3b12daee45876b0129a3602dc8f534ce30bf0","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGJlYTNiMTJkYWVlNDU4NzZiMDEyOWEzNjAyZGM4ZjUzNGNlMzBiZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T04:09:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T13:41:50Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: support a non-unified KV cache in QSA\n\nset_input_qsa asserted n_stream == 1, so llama-server could not serve this\nmodel with more than one slot unless -kvu was passed. With a non-unified\ncache each sequence owns its own cells, and a cell index means a different\ntoken in each stream, so a single shared mapping is wrong.\n\n- cell_blk, blk_cells and bias gain a stream dimension. At n_stream == 1\n  these collapse to the shapes they had, so the unified path is unchanged.\n- Scoring is now batched over streams. ggml_mul_mat matches ne[2] on both\n  operands, so stream s's queries only ever meet stream s's blocks; without\n  this sequences would score against each other's context.\n- set_input_qsa loops per stream and resolves cells through\n  v_cells[seq_to_stream[seq_id]], following set_input_kq_mask_impl, instead\n  of hardcoding v_cells[0].\n- llama_kv_cache_context::get_n_stream() is added, mirroring the ns that\n  get_k and get_v already derive from the slot info.\n\nbuild_attn_mask_top_k needed no change: it already expects\n[n_top_k, n_batch, 1, n_stream], so the top-k result is reshaped to meet it.\n\nset_input_qsa has exactly one caller, so the blast radius is qwen4exp only.\n\nValidation, UD-Q4_K_XL on one B200:\n\n- unified cache unchanged within noise: 1802.9/68.85 -> 1807.2/69.11 t/s at\n  batch 1, 2262.5/192.43 -> 2270.1/193.75 at batch 4.\n- non-unified now runs at npl 1, 4, 16 where it previously aborted, and is\n  22% faster than the -kvu workaround at batch 16 (1205 vs 984 t/s total),\n  since per-stream cells avoid the cross-sequence masking a unified cache\n  pays for.\n- no cross-stream contamination: four concurrent sequences each carrying a\n  distinct secret all recall their own and no other, on both cache modes.\n- test-llama-archs green on qwen4exp, deepseek2, gemma3n, qwen3next, llama.\n\nNote on testing: comparing concurrent output against solo output exactly is\nnot a valid check. It failed 0/4 with no bug present, and the unified-cache\ncontrol failed the same way, because batch composition changes the\nfloating-point reduction order and near-tied tokens flip. The contamination\ntest above is what the exit code gates on.","tree":{"sha":"7d83cf3d00eb76968544eb3a7e138676d366243b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/7d83cf3d00eb76968544eb3a7e138676d366243b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/bea3b12daee45876b0129a3602dc8f534ce30bf0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/bea3b12daee45876b0129a3602dc8f534ce30bf0","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/bea3b12daee45876b0129a3602dc8f534ce30bf0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/bea3b12daee45876b0129a3602dc8f534ce30bf0/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"eb95d125bad0b8d302717a7a55e61845da9e7883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/eb95d125bad0b8d302717a7a55e61845da9e7883","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/eb95d125bad0b8d302717a7a55e61845da9e7883"}]},{"sha":"7fee670a95eb545a7795e46a04d5a4a8d5f238f8","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDdmZWU2NzBhOTVlYjU0NWE3Nzk1ZTQ2YTA0ZDVhNGE4ZDVmMjM4Zjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T14:42:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T15:09:53Z"},"message":"llama: keep the qwen4exp top-k attention mask arch-local\n\nThe QSA graph needed a build_attn that attends only to the cells named by a\ntop_k tensor, and the first version got it by adding a llm_graph_input_attn_kv\noverload to llm_graph_context and factoring the mask construction out of the\nexisting MLA sparse path into a shared build_attn_mask_top_k.\n\nThat put a new arch on the shared attention path and made the deepseek32 and\nglm-dsa attention build depend on a helper introduced for qwen4exp. Build the\nmask in src/models/qwen4exp.cpp instead and leave llama-graph.{h,cpp} exactly as\nthey were: the MLA path keeps its own copy of the same node sequence.\n\nThe nodes emitted are unchanged, so this is bit-identical.","tree":{"sha":"47db728c956fbff339851c7f7830ed1d0ecd43a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/47db728c956fbff339851c7f7830ed1d0ecd43a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/7fee670a95eb545a7795e46a04d5a4a8d5f238f8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/7fee670a95eb545a7795e46a04d5a4a8d5f238f8","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/7fee670a95eb545a7795e46a04d5a4a8d5f238f8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/7fee670a95eb545a7795e46a04d5a4a8d5f238f8/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bea3b12daee45876b0129a3602dc8f534ce30bf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/bea3b12daee45876b0129a3602dc8f534ce30bf0","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/bea3b12daee45876b0129a3602dc8f534ce30bf0"}]},{"sha":"035e22731a7fd70b9854b3a2d64ec68e9b1a45d3","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDAzNWUyMjczMWE3ZmQ3MGI5ODU0YjNhMmQ2NGVjNjhlOWIxYTQ1ZDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T14:43:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T15:09:53Z"},"message":"llama: hold the qwen4exp indexer cache in a new llama_memory_hybrid_idx\n\nThe indexer key cache was added by extending llama_memory_hybrid with an\noptional third cache, and the host-side cell/block mapping that drives QSA was\nadded as set_input_qsa on llama_kv_cache. Both are shared classes that every\nhybrid and every attention model goes through.\n\nMove both into a new memory type, llama_memory_hybrid_idx, following\nllama_kv_cache_msa: the indexer cache and the pos<->cell translation live with\nthe sparse-attention memory rather than in the classes that serve every other\narchitecture. llama-kv-cache.{h,cpp} and llama-memory-hybrid.{h,cpp} are\nrestored to their unmodified state.\n\ninit_batch is repeated from llama_memory_hybrid because the indexer cache has to\nbe handed the attention cache's slot infos, and those are not reachable through\nthe context the base returns. Allocating them separately lets the two caches\ndrift, which is what pointed QSA's top-k at the wrong cells before.\n\nThe context derives from llama_memory_hybrid_context so build_inp_mem_hybrid\nkeeps working unchanged, and get_n_stream is computed from the slot infos\nexactly as llama_kv_cache_context did.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged: logits over an 8192-token sequence are bit-identical to\nthe previous implementation, sparse and dense alike.","tree":{"sha":"c946a1b3c9fbc8c0b1313eb77b48d34d8ce1884f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/c946a1b3c9fbc8c0b1313eb77b48d34d8ce1884f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/035e22731a7fd70b9854b3a2d64ec68e9b1a45d3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/035e22731a7fd70b9854b3a2d64ec68e9b1a45d3","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/035e22731a7fd70b9854b3a2d64ec68e9b1a45d3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/035e22731a7fd70b9854b3a2d64ec68e9b1a45d3/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7fee670a95eb545a7795e46a04d5a4a8d5f238f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/7fee670a95eb545a7795e46a04d5a4a8d5f238f8","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/7fee670a95eb545a7795e46a04d5a4a8d5f238f8"}]},{"sha":"cfbdc0a50d127893ce51369a7e1659f7537f778b","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGNmYmRjMGE1MGQxMjc4OTNjZTUxMzY5YTdlMTY1OWY3NTM3Zjc3OGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T15:06:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T00:45:01Z"},"message":"llama: save and restore the qwen4exp indexer KV cache\n\nllama_memory_hybrid_idx forwarded clear, seq_rm, seq_cp, seq_keep, seq_add and\nseq_div to the indexer cache but not state_write / state_read, so a saved\nsession dropped the indexer keys and a restored one selected QSA top-k against\nan empty cache. The effect is invisible until the context passes\nindexer_top_k + compress_ratio - 1 cells, because QSA is exactly dense below\nthat and the indexer contents cannot change the result.\n\nThe indexer section is written last rather than next to the attention cache it\nmirrors. As a suffix, a reader that does not expect it stops early and the\ntrailing bytes are caught by the size check in state_load_file; placed between\nthe attention and recurrent sections it would instead be parsed as recurrent\nstate, which can succeed and restore silent garbage. It follows the same\nLLAMA_STATE_SEQ_FLAGS_PARTIAL_ONLY gate as the attention cache, since a partial\ncheckpoint deliberately skips the token-level attention caches.\n\nThe indexer restores its own cells instead of taking the attention cache's\nrestored slots. The two caches share size, padding and every sequence\noperation, and init_batch hands the indexer the attention cache's slot infos,\nso both state_read_meta calls run find_slot over identical occupancy and land\non identical cells.\n\nThe overrides live on llama_memory_hybrid_idx, the only memory type that owns\nan indexer cache, so llama_memory_hybrid and every architecture that uses it\nwrite and read exactly the bytes they did before.\n\nThe session and sequence state versions are bumped because the qwen4exp state\nlayout changed. The session path already rejects a short read via its size\ncheck, but llama_state_seq_load_file accepts one silently, so only the version\ncheck stops a pre-fix blob from being half-restored by a fixed build.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 2721542354f8e158c3217625f4e2e7b83e51e3fe)","tree":{"sha":"4dfc0bc0e00c2631a53ec76ca27af225e14ce2cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/4dfc0bc0e00c2631a53ec76ca27af225e14ce2cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/cfbdc0a50d127893ce51369a7e1659f7537f778b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/cfbdc0a50d127893ce51369a7e1659f7537f778b","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/cfbdc0a50d127893ce51369a7e1659f7537f778b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/cfbdc0a50d127893ce51369a7e1659f7537f778b/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"035e22731a7fd70b9854b3a2d64ec68e9b1a45d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/035e22731a7fd70b9854b3a2d64ec68e9b1a45d3","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/035e22731a7fd70b9854b3a2d64ec68e9b1a45d3"}]},{"sha":"d22d2be2b47703ad6323cc805295ac9762ef4f1c","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGQyMmQyYmUyYjQ3NzAzYWQ2MzIzY2M4MDUyOTVhYzk3NjJlZjRmMWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T15:15:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T00:45:01Z"},"message":"llama: make the qwen4exp PLE n-gram history per context and serialise it\n\nThe PLE hash of a token mixes in the ple_ngram_size - 1 tokens before it, which\na decode ubatch does not carry, so they were remembered in a map on\nllama_model_qwen4exp. That is the wrong owner twice over.\n\nA llama_model is shared by every context that loads it, and the map was keyed\nonly by llama_seq_id, so two contexts running the same sequence id - two server\ninstances on one model, or a draft/target pair - overwrote each other's window.\nThe next_pos guard turned that into EOS padding instead of a crash, so it\ndegraded quality silently.\n\nThe map was also in no state blob: grep found ple_hist in neither\nllama-kv-cache.cpp nor llama-memory-*.cpp nor llama-context.cpp. A restored\ncontext therefore failed the next_pos check on its first ubatch and hashed the\nfirst tokens after the restore against EOS padding. This is why a session blob\nround-tripped byte for byte while the restored context computed different\nlogits: the state was never in the bytes.\n\nIt moves to llama_memory_hybrid_idx, which is per context, is the memory type\nqwen4exp always builds, and already does the per-sequence bookkeeping this\nneeds. Every sequence operation now carries the window with it:\n\n  seq_rm   a rewind (p1 < 0) truncates the window to the surviving prefix and\n           moves next_pos to p0, so a rollback keeps exact context; a hole\n           punched in the middle leaves the window non-contiguous, so it is\n           dropped\n  seq_cp   the destination inherits the source's window, truncated to the\n           copied position range - a copied sequence continues with the same\n           n-grams the source would have used\n  seq_keep every other sequence's window is dropped, like its cells\n  seq_add  a shift that moves the whole window keeps it and moves next_pos with\n           it, which is the context-shift case; one that cuts through it drops\n           it\n  seq_div  positions stop being consecutive, so an overlapping window is\n           dropped\n  clear    everything is dropped\n\nDropping means next_pos = -1, which set_input turns into full EOS padding: the\nsame thing a fresh sequence gets, and the same thing this code did before it\nfollowed the sequence operations at all, so no case is worse than before.\n\nThe state payload is a self-delimiting list, u32 count then per entry\n{ i32 seq_id, i32 next_pos, u32 n_toks, i32 toks[n_toks] }, so a whole-context\nsave and a single-sequence save share one format and a single-sequence restore\ncan retarget the window at its destination seq_id. It is written after the\nindexer section, last, for the same reason that one is: as a pure suffix an\nolder reader stops early instead of parsing these bytes as something else.\n\nUnlike the indexer section it is not under LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_FLAGS_PARTIAL_ONLY.\nThe window is recurrent state - it is the input the PLE convolution's own\nrecurrent state is derived from - and the recurrent cache beside it is written\nfor partial checkpoints too. Gating it would leave the server's speculative\ndecoding checkpoints restoring the conv state without the window that produced\nit.\n\nNo further version bump: LLAMA_SESSION_VERSION 10 and LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_VERSION 3\nwere introduced for the indexer section in the same unreleased series, and both\nchanges are qwen4exp-only additions to the same blob layout.\n\nAlso fixes the padding of a short window. set_input pads a window shorter than\nngram_size - 1 up to that length, but prev() indexes the snapshot with the most\nrecent token last, and resize() pads at the back, so the filler EOS landed where\nthe immediately preceding token belongs. It now pads at the front. A window is\nshort at a sequence start after a one-token prefill, and after a seq_rm rewind,\nwhich the new bookkeeping makes common.\n\nEvery architecture other than qwen4exp builds llama_memory_hybrid rather than\nllama_memory_hybrid_idx, has no PLE table and never asks for a history, so\nnothing about its graph, its sequence operations or its state bytes changes.\n\n(cherry picked from commit de170364c052c68fcf63285cc0028095edb9f23c)","tree":{"sha":"3a496a1a413a084d0ad425fe4da9947a48c65fbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/3a496a1a413a084d0ad425fe4da9947a48c65fbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/d22d2be2b47703ad6323cc805295ac9762ef4f1c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/d22d2be2b47703ad6323cc805295ac9762ef4f1c","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/d22d2be2b47703ad6323cc805295ac9762ef4f1c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/d22d2be2b47703ad6323cc805295ac9762ef4f1c/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cfbdc0a50d127893ce51369a7e1659f7537f778b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/cfbdc0a50d127893ce51369a7e1659f7537f778b","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/cfbdc0a50d127893ce51369a7e1659f7537f778b"}]},{"sha":"d4a943f9a521dc2f50e401b7565f8dc5abe3b568","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGQ0YTk0M2Y5YTUyMWRjMmY1MGU0MDFiNzU2NWY4ZGM1YWJlM2I1Njg","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T15:46:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T00:45:01Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: tidy comments and simplify image token read\n\nRewrite the comments this series adds to the AGENTS.md rules: one or two lines,\nno prose hard-wrapped mid-sentence, no narrative or history, and no comment that\nonly restates the code. Net 146 fewer comment lines, no code change.\n\nCorrect the PLE image comment: mtmd does not consume the placeholder ids. An\nimage is decoded as an embeddings-only batch, so ubatch->token is null and the\nper-position ids never exist here. gemma3n and gemma4 hit the same case and\nstand in row 0 of per_layer_token_embd; qwen4exp stands in the configured image\ntoken id instead.\n\nRead image_token_id straight from self.hparams in the converter. base.py merges\ntext_config into the root of hparams, and the key sits at the root of\nconfig.json, so the config.json re-read was redundant.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 205840c12169057da3e8d2f65ec4ceec3e18b980)","tree":{"sha":"c593863c23a518bf8a3a138ebf3f67ab06103f50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/c593863c23a518bf8a3a138ebf3f67ab06103f50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/d4a943f9a521dc2f50e401b7565f8dc5abe3b568","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/d4a943f9a521dc2f50e401b7565f8dc5abe3b568","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/d4a943f9a521dc2f50e401b7565f8dc5abe3b568","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/d4a943f9a521dc2f50e401b7565f8dc5abe3b568/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d22d2be2b47703ad6323cc805295ac9762ef4f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/d22d2be2b47703ad6323cc805295ac9762ef4f1c","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/d22d2be2b47703ad6323cc805295ac9762ef4f1c"}]},{"sha":"0ac4b18025c2e255dd76252cd3b465683d08b257","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDBhYzRiMTgwMjVjMmUyNTVkZDc2MjUyY2QzYjQ2NTY4M2QwOGIyNTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T16:13:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T00:45:01Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: support a quantized KV cache in the QSA attention path\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4c30574f81dc1115d08078c47b6cf8c789c0a842)","tree":{"sha":"2aa80accf3062d27a4d379dff69cd2cbca8285f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/2aa80accf3062d27a4d379dff69cd2cbca8285f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/0ac4b18025c2e255dd76252cd3b465683d08b257","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/0ac4b18025c2e255dd76252cd3b465683d08b257","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/0ac4b18025c2e255dd76252cd3b465683d08b257","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/0ac4b18025c2e255dd76252cd3b465683d08b257/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d4a943f9a521dc2f50e401b7565f8dc5abe3b568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/d4a943f9a521dc2f50e401b7565f8dc5abe3b568","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/d4a943f9a521dc2f50e401b7565f8dc5abe3b568"}]},{"sha":"c52ed2a0b0b865e82eb1b393106c48df1c39cb32","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGM1MmVkMmEwYjBiODY1ZTgyZWIxYjM5MzEwNmM0OGRmMWMzOWNiMzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T17:37:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T00:45:01Z"},"message":"llama: give qwen4exp a large-graph node budget\n\n(cherry picked from commit 37c8c194e6a30e4c46ac29bee3fb264f091596ef)","tree":{"sha":"a8ed854a689c39d195ee2c99834b6bff3ecd82fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/a8ed854a689c39d195ee2c99834b6bff3ecd82fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/c52ed2a0b0b865e82eb1b393106c48df1c39cb32","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c52ed2a0b0b865e82eb1b393106c48df1c39cb32","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/c52ed2a0b0b865e82eb1b393106c48df1c39cb32","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c52ed2a0b0b865e82eb1b393106c48df1c39cb32/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0ac4b18025c2e255dd76252cd3b465683d08b257","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/0ac4b18025c2e255dd76252cd3b465683d08b257","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/0ac4b18025c2e255dd76252cd3b465683d08b257"}]},{"sha":"6a69a0c12c771aaa057ee16c21bbbc879bfa671c","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDZhNjlhMGMxMmM3NzFhYWEwNTdlZTE2YzIxYmJiYzg3OWJmYTY3MWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T00:00:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T00:45:01Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: drop an unused variable that breaks -Werror builds\n\n(cherry picked from commit 528d032b51fa3cf935ed3ef6e0fb1c7401df53b5)","tree":{"sha":"393932a09912b7238302242ade5ee4ca85e76232","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/393932a09912b7238302242ade5ee4ca85e76232"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/6a69a0c12c771aaa057ee16c21bbbc879bfa671c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6a69a0c12c771aaa057ee16c21bbbc879bfa671c","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/6a69a0c12c771aaa057ee16c21bbbc879bfa671c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6a69a0c12c771aaa057ee16c21bbbc879bfa671c/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c52ed2a0b0b865e82eb1b393106c48df1c39cb32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/c52ed2a0b0b865e82eb1b393106c48df1c39cb32","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/c52ed2a0b0b865e82eb1b393106c48df1c39cb32"}]},{"sha":"ef9fa1ba1f0d3f11ed7ddc1da94e5db4c22ae7b6","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGVmOWZhMWJhMWYwZDNmMTFlZDdkZGMxZGE5NGU1ZGI0YzIyYWU3YjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-26T17:18:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T00:45:01Z"},"message":"quantize: dequantize and quantize large tensors in row bands\n\nf32_conv_buf held the whole dequantized tensor, which is 204.8 GB for\nper_layer_token_embd alone and dies with std::bad_alloc long before the\nwork buffer is reached. Dequantize and quantize in bands of whole rows\ninstead, capping the f32 staging at 1 GiB per band.\n\nRows are independent and the imatrix is indexed by column, so band\nboundaries cannot change any output byte. Bands nest inside the existing\nper-expert loop so each expert slice keeps its own imatrix, and a band is\nkept to at least one quantization chunk per worker thread so the existing\nmultithreading still has work. F32 sources still stage nothing and are\nbanded by pointer arithmetic into the tensor.\n\nllama_tensor_dequantize_impl now takes a first element offset; the single\ncaller is updated.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 658c22549613555dbce57a772be4de8509eba3ee)","tree":{"sha":"f68fdf3dc11148d927df89a9bb10a182b87a168e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/f68fdf3dc11148d927df89a9bb10a182b87a168e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/ef9fa1ba1f0d3f11ed7ddc1da94e5db4c22ae7b6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ef9fa1ba1f0d3f11ed7ddc1da94e5db4c22ae7b6","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/ef9fa1ba1f0d3f11ed7ddc1da94e5db4c22ae7b6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ef9fa1ba1f0d3f11ed7ddc1da94e5db4c22ae7b6/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6a69a0c12c771aaa057ee16c21bbbc879bfa671c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6a69a0c12c771aaa057ee16c21bbbc879bfa671c","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/6a69a0c12c771aaa057ee16c21bbbc879bfa671c"}]},{"sha":"5674c73aa8f46ba41c3401828fb2615c623c0f2f","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDU2NzRjNzNhYThmNDZiYTQxYzM0MDE4MjhmYjI2MTVjNjIzYzBmMmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T01:14:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T01:42:08Z"},"message":"llama: segment the qwen4exp fused QKV for tensor split\n\nqwen4exp was missing from the gated delta net branch of get_split_segments,\nso its attn_qkv.weight, shaped {n_embd, 2*key_dim + value_dim}, fell through\nto the generic fused QKV rule and tripped\nGGML_ASSERT(tensor->ne[axis] == n_embd + 2*n_embd_gqa) while loading with\n--split-mode tensor. --split-mode layer was unaffected.\n\nqwen4exp broadcasts K to the V heads by tiling, k_conv is grown with a plain\nggml_repeat_4d over the head axis so that v head j pairs with k head\nj % n_k_heads. That is the Qwen 3.5 pattern, not the repeat interleave that\nQwen 3 Next builds explicitly, so qwen4exp takes the else branch and its V is\nsegmented on the scale of K.\n\nReported by benklop.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 353d753f595dc81634ae6130188b31f06018f5ae)","tree":{"sha":"274a23d8bd7d4350dce493e965868f95815ce964","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/274a23d8bd7d4350dce493e965868f95815ce964"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/5674c73aa8f46ba41c3401828fb2615c623c0f2f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/5674c73aa8f46ba41c3401828fb2615c623c0f2f","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/5674c73aa8f46ba41c3401828fb2615c623c0f2f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/5674c73aa8f46ba41c3401828fb2615c623c0f2f/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ef9fa1ba1f0d3f11ed7ddc1da94e5db4c22ae7b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/ef9fa1ba1f0d3f11ed7ddc1da94e5db4c22ae7b6","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/ef9fa1ba1f0d3f11ed7ddc1da94e5db4c22ae7b6"}]},{"sha":"24ea62df446cf698c5b4c5fa494b462ad7adf490","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDI0ZWE2MmRmNDQ2Y2Y2OThjNWI0YzVmYTQ5NGI0NjJhZDdhZGY0OTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T01:18:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T01:42:33Z"},"message":"llama: fix the qwen4exp PLE history seq_rm(-1) iterator invalidation and the fatal-warning build\n\nple_hist_rm recursed over ple_hist with a range-based for and the recursive call\nerases the entry it is iterating when the whole sequence is removed (p0 <= 0,\np1 < 0), so the loop then increments an invalidated iterator. It is unreachable\ntoday only because llama_memory_recurrent::seq_rm rejects seq_id < 0 before\nllama_memory_hybrid_idx::seq_rm reaches the history, which is a guard in another\nclass. Advance past the entry before recursing.\n\nTwo smaller things in the same area:\n\n  - the n_toks sanity bound in ple_hist_state_read was the literal 64, which is\n    the value of LLAMA_MAX_PLE_HEADS, not of the quantity being checked. The\n    window is at most ple_ngram_size - 1 tokens, so the bound is\n    LLAMA_MAX_PLE_NGRAM - 1, eight times tighter.\n\n  - build_conv_state_at left mem_size unused, so -DLLAMA_FATAL_WARNINGS=ON does\n    not compile. Predates this series; drop the line.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 6eba44a89d5f328eb4859b844e1d28fb564cbe3e)","tree":{"sha":"b99ff720e5297c14ea45946aad36bbf1967a81f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/b99ff720e5297c14ea45946aad36bbf1967a81f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/24ea62df446cf698c5b4c5fa494b462ad7adf490","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/24ea62df446cf698c5b4c5fa494b462ad7adf490","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/24ea62df446cf698c5b4c5fa494b462ad7adf490","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/24ea62df446cf698c5b4c5fa494b462ad7adf490/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5674c73aa8f46ba41c3401828fb2615c623c0f2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/5674c73aa8f46ba41c3401828fb2615c623c0f2f","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/5674c73aa8f46ba41c3401828fb2615c623c0f2f"}]},{"sha":"0b19188e935480369f3b006e0cf17576dce066a3","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDBiMTkxODhlOTM1NDgwMzY5ZjNiMDA2ZTBjZjE3NTc2ZGNlMDY2YTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T01:09:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T01:42:33Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: include llama-impl.h explicitly for llama_mul_mat_hadamard\n\n(cherry picked from commit b634fd4d250d181ef82bf78bd00c1ae3b96a7af6)","tree":{"sha":"ad17144c033e5dec8959c7c04060d912d10bdb31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/ad17144c033e5dec8959c7c04060d912d10bdb31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/0b19188e935480369f3b006e0cf17576dce066a3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/0b19188e935480369f3b006e0cf17576dce066a3","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/0b19188e935480369f3b006e0cf17576dce066a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/0b19188e935480369f3b006e0cf17576dce066a3/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"24ea62df446cf698c5b4c5fa494b462ad7adf490","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/24ea62df446cf698c5b4c5fa494b462ad7adf490","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/24ea62df446cf698c5b4c5fa494b462ad7adf490"}]},{"sha":"213df585b9aed6a09be30d8401f267bf603c104c","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDIxM2RmNTg1YjlhZWQ2YTA5YmUzMGQ4NDAxZjI2N2JmNjAzYzEwNGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T02:26:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T02:26:31Z"},"message":"convert: fix the qwen4exp lint and type-check failures\n\nflake8 flagged an unused MmprojModel import, and ty flagged seven errors in\nthe PLE streaming path: eos_token_id can be absent, and _ple_map, _ple_path,\n_ple_row_dim and _ple_rows_per_shard are all Optional at the declaration but\nwere dereferenced without narrowing.\n\nThe map is opened and the stride fixed before the first shard is written, and\n_finish_ple_table only runs once every shard has landed, so the invariants\nhold. Assert them so the checker can see it. A missing eos_token_id now raises\nwith the reason instead of a TypeError from int(None).","tree":{"sha":"a7010cf2fc752bffd86ccaaa72dd7bbae0e24b39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/a7010cf2fc752bffd86ccaaa72dd7bbae0e24b39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/213df585b9aed6a09be30d8401f267bf603c104c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/213df585b9aed6a09be30d8401f267bf603c104c","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/213df585b9aed6a09be30d8401f267bf603c104c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/213df585b9aed6a09be30d8401f267bf603c104c/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0b19188e935480369f3b006e0cf17576dce066a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/0b19188e935480369f3b006e0cf17576dce066a3","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/0b19188e935480369f3b006e0cf17576dce066a3"}]},{"sha":"fbe17732bdbf594a0d6cc046fc15d7357cdbf75a","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGZiZTE3NzMyYmRiZjU5NGEwZDZjYzA0NmZjMTVkNzM1N2NkYmY3NWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T03:41:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T03:58:12Z"},"message":"llama: give the qwen4exp indexer cache its own tensor names\n\nThe indexer KV cache and the attention KV cache both named their tensors\ncache_k_l%d, so the Meta backend matched the indexer cache against the\nattention split pattern and aborted in handle_set_rows. Tag the names\ninstead, and mirror the indexer cache: it has one key head and its\nprojections are mirrored.\n\n(cherry picked from commit a1cdc8181134659766763a17762545a1f0e5db7b)","tree":{"sha":"6fa0d8d73a0155b594e706fb002a45ab3e29c0c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/6fa0d8d73a0155b594e706fb002a45ab3e29c0c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/fbe17732bdbf594a0d6cc046fc15d7357cdbf75a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/fbe17732bdbf594a0d6cc046fc15d7357cdbf75a","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/fbe17732bdbf594a0d6cc046fc15d7357cdbf75a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/fbe17732bdbf594a0d6cc046fc15d7357cdbf75a/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"213df585b9aed6a09be30d8401f267bf603c104c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/213df585b9aed6a09be30d8401f267bf603c104c","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/213df585b9aed6a09be30d8401f267bf603c104c"}]},{"sha":"6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDZjNWFmYzg2YWU4NDQ0OGFlNGQ3NDRlMzU3MDE3ZTJjNDkwYWQ5YzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"danielhanchen","email":"unslothshared@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T03:47:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T03:58:12Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: double the Q split granularity for tensor parallelism\n\nqwen4exp fuses the attention gate into attn_q.weight the same way qwen3next\nand qwen 3.5 do, so a device boundary must fall on a whole q+gate pair or the\nQ heads stop lining up with the K/V heads and attn_output rows.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 6c9a592f0a425a459ab6efae3b897cf68460e244)","tree":{"sha":"96f89b8034b2b2e2eb2713b404f884e06b56902b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/96f89b8034b2b2e2eb2713b404f884e06b56902b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fbe17732bdbf594a0d6cc046fc15d7357cdbf75a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/fbe17732bdbf594a0d6cc046fc15d7357cdbf75a","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/fbe17732bdbf594a0d6cc046fc15d7357cdbf75a"}]},{"sha":"8b3ed0a400ad0bbd5d567e313b6cf5358178b723","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKDhiM2VkMGE0MDBhZDBiYmQ1ZDU2N2UzMTNiNmNmNTM1ODE3OGI3MjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T02:35:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T06:23:08Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: keep the indexer cache in step across server slots\n\nThe QSA indexer keeps a side cache addressed by the cells of the attention\ncache, so cell j has to hold the same token in both: the top-k indices it\nproduces are applied to the attention KQ mask. init_batch already hands the\nindexer the attention cache's slot layout rather than letting it look for its\nown, but the restore path did not. state_read called llama_kv_cache::state_read\non the two caches in turn and each ran its own find_slot over its own occupancy.\nThat agrees only for as long as nothing has already pushed the two caches apart,\nwhich is the property a restore is supposed to re-establish rather than one it\ncan lean on.\n\nThe failure path was the worse half, and it is reachable from the public API\nwith nothing more than a short buffer. Truncating a good blob at 35 offsets and\nfeeding it to llama_state_seq_set_data left the two caches disagreeing at 5 of\nthem, and every one of 23 truncations of a whole-context blob did. Four of those\nfive land inside the attention section, so the attention cache drops the\nsequence and the indexer keeps it; only the cut that lands in the indexer\nsection gives the opposite direction. llama_kv_cache::state_read cleans up its\nown cache and rethrows, so whichever way it falls, nothing is left to bring the\ntwo back together. The server papers over this by clearing the slot when a\nprompt cache load fails; a caller of llama_state_seq_set_data that does not is\nleft with an indexer addressing cells that no longer mean what it thinks.\n\nllama_kv_cache::state_read_sinfo reports the cells a restore landed in, or takes\na copy of them, and state_read_meta uses a supplied layout in place of find_slot\nonce it has checked that those cells are free here too. The indexer now adopts\nthe attention cache's restored layout by construction instead of reproducing it\nby coincidence, and a layout that does not fit fails the read rather than being\napplied over cells that already drifted. The hybrid restore is wrapped so that\nany failure drops the sequence, or for a whole-context restore the context, from\nall three caches at once, which is a state they do agree on.","tree":{"sha":"95cb9cda58c84039f2bda847e00bddacbd10d916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/95cb9cda58c84039f2bda847e00bddacbd10d916"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/8b3ed0a400ad0bbd5d567e313b6cf5358178b723","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/8b3ed0a400ad0bbd5d567e313b6cf5358178b723","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/8b3ed0a400ad0bbd5d567e313b6cf5358178b723","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/8b3ed0a400ad0bbd5d567e313b6cf5358178b723/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3"}]},{"sha":"f43070aa5cc52cae7ddaefc43625357a6b88269d","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGY0MzA3MGFhNWNjNTJjYWU3ZGRhZWZjNDM2MjUzNTdhNmI4ODI2OWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T04:13:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T06:23:08Z"},"message":"kv-cache: clear the cache once when restoring a whole context\n\nstate_read walks the streams of the cache in turn, and for a whole-context restore\neach stream went through state_read_meta, which starts by calling clear(). clear()\nresets every stream at once, so each stream after the first threw away the streams\nalready restored, and the K/V buffers with them. A non-unified cache holds one\nstream per sequence, so a context saved with N sequences in it came back with only\nthe sequence in the last stream that carried any cells - the highest sequence id.\nA unified cache has one stream and never showed it.\n\nThe cache is now emptied once, before the loop, which is what a whole-context\nrestore means. A blob whose streams are all empty now empties the cache as well,\nwhere before it left the old contents in place.","tree":{"sha":"ae97fe5d641aa6d6dbf9c263295eb817085d1f94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/ae97fe5d641aa6d6dbf9c263295eb817085d1f94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/f43070aa5cc52cae7ddaefc43625357a6b88269d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/f43070aa5cc52cae7ddaefc43625357a6b88269d","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/f43070aa5cc52cae7ddaefc43625357a6b88269d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/f43070aa5cc52cae7ddaefc43625357a6b88269d/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8b3ed0a400ad0bbd5d567e313b6cf5358178b723","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/8b3ed0a400ad0bbd5d567e313b6cf5358178b723","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/8b3ed0a400ad0bbd5d567e313b6cf5358178b723"}]},{"sha":"d1fe507f9526fddbdc87760a74b1e5dc906395f1","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGQxZmU1MDdmOTUyNmZkZGJkYzg3NzYwYTc0YjFlNWRjOTA2Mzk1ZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T04:13:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T06:23:08Z"},"message":"kv-cache: check the mirrored slot layout on a whole-context restore too\n\nstate_read_meta only looked at the layout it was given on the single-sequence path.\nA whole-context restore lays the cells out from 0 in both caches, so they agree as\nlong as they restore the same number of cells, but nothing checked that they did: an\nindexer section belonging to some other context was read over cells the attention\ncache had filled from a different one, which is the state the indexer must never be\nleft in.","tree":{"sha":"3058aa2dde318ad094117a71545df76643ee264f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/3058aa2dde318ad094117a71545df76643ee264f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/d1fe507f9526fddbdc87760a74b1e5dc906395f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/d1fe507f9526fddbdc87760a74b1e5dc906395f1","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/d1fe507f9526fddbdc87760a74b1e5dc906395f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/d1fe507f9526fddbdc87760a74b1e5dc906395f1/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f43070aa5cc52cae7ddaefc43625357a6b88269d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/f43070aa5cc52cae7ddaefc43625357a6b88269d","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/f43070aa5cc52cae7ddaefc43625357a6b88269d"}]},{"sha":"bf5396021efd91b2a2253aa620a270e87d8955b5","node_id":"C_kwDOMU0YaNoAKGJmNTM5NjAyMWVmZDkxYjJhMjI1M2FhNjIwYTI3MGU4N2Q4OTU1YjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T04:42:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"Daniel Han","email":"danielhanchen@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-27T06:23:08Z"},"message":"qwen4exp: give the PLE conv history its own mirrored recurrent row\n\nn_embd_r() reserved n_conv + ple_conv_state() so that one cache_r_l row could\ncarry both the delta-net conv state and the PLE dilated conv history, but the\nQWEN4EXP arm of get_split_segments only described n_conv. Under -sm tensor the\nsegment sum came up short by ple_conv_state() and llama_memory_recurrent\nconstruction aborted in ggml_backend_meta_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft.\n\nWidening the segment list is not the fix. The Meta backend propagates a view's\nsplit descriptor from its parent unchanged, so a view of one sub-range of a\nsplit axis is sized as the whole row on every device; declaring the PLE tail as\na second segment merely moves the abort to \"shape mismatch for VIEW\" at graph\nallocation. The two histories also want opposite policies: the delta-net state\nis split by head to match wqkv and ssm_conv1d, while per_layer_tok_embd,\nple_conv1d and ple_norm_conv are all mirrored, so every device computes the\nwhole dilated conv and needs the whole history. One tensor cannot be both, and\nthe split state has no per-segment mirroring.\n\nMove the PLE history into its own cache_ple_r_l%d row, mark it MIRRORED, and\nreturn n_embd_r() to n_conv. The row is allocated only on layers where is_ple\nholds, so mirroring one 92160-element row per device replaces a 92160-element\ntail on all 36 recurrent rows: the recurrent R footprint drops rather than\ngrows. build_conv_state_at now takes its width from the tensor it was handed\nand keys its gather on that tensor, which also drops a cont of a strided view.","tree":{"sha":"d03207fcb8ed59cad9ba71c623d42c5e8099f89a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/trees/d03207fcb8ed59cad9ba71c623d42c5e8099f89a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/commits/bf5396021efd91b2a2253aa620a270e87d8955b5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/bf5396021efd91b2a2253aa620a270e87d8955b5","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/bf5396021efd91b2a2253aa620a270e87d8955b5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/bf5396021efd91b2a2253aa620a270e87d8955b5/comments","author":{"login":"danielhanchen","id":23090290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDkwMjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23090290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen","html_url":"https://github.com/danielhanchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielhanchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/u